    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Note that, by (1), f is uniquely determined by the values f(1),... ,f(n), which are pairwise distinct modulo n. We often simply denote f = [f(1),... ,f(n)]. Note also that, upon the presence of (1) and (2), (3) is equivalent to |{i ∈ [n] : f(i) > n}| = k. We denote the set of (k,n)-bounded aﬃne permutations by BA(k,n). We say that f is a bounded n-aﬃne permutation if there exists k such that f is a (k,n)-bounded aﬃne permutation."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 14,
    "page number" : 1,
