    "bounding box" : [ 85.078, 81.407, 527.071, 132.381 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Now, we associate a Grassmann necklace and a bounded aﬃne permutation to an element V in the Grassmannian Gr(k,n) following [19, 24]. We represent V by a k ×n matrix of rank k, up to row operations, and denote by v1,... ,vn ∈ Ck the columns of V . Furthermore, we deﬁne vi for all i ∈ Z by setting vi+n := (−1)k−1vi. Given an (ordered) k-element subset"
  } ]
